<title>FRANCE: New York heads Paris H1 air export cargo listing.</title>
<headline>New York heads Paris H1 air export cargo listing.</headline>
<dateline>PARIS 1997-07-31</dateline>
<text>
<p>The Paris airports authority said New York was the top export destination from Charles de Gaulle and Orly Airports in January-June 1997.</p>
<p>The top ten ex-Paris air cargo destinations, in tonnes, in first half 1997, with the percentage change on Jan-Jun '96 were:</p>
<p>	  Origin   Jan-June '97  Pct Change</p>
<p>    1.  New York     17,976   down  4.2</p>
<p>    2.  Chicago	13,985     up  5.4</p>
<p>    3.  Tokyo	  12,410   down  8.7</p>
<p>    4.  Hong Kong    12,356     up 11.7</p>
<p>    5.  Mexico City  6,524	up 17.2</p>
<p>    6.  Montreal     6,321    down  3.9</p>
<p>    7.  Sao Paulo    6,239	up 20.2</p>
<p>    8.  Singapore    5,594	up 39.9</p>
<p>    9.  Los Angeles  4,930    down 19.6</p>
<p>   10.  Miami	  4,180	up  5.4</p>
<p>- Reuters Air Cargo Service Tel+ 44 171 542 7706 Fax +5017 - www.racs.com</p>
